Z||000000||trigger||03-16-2001||03:06 PM||||I was wondering if anybody could supply me with any historical information on the car? it's for an english paper i'm writing.  I also need to know the source of the info.  thanks in advance.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000001||Oreif||03-16-2001||06:12 PM||||Just get the Gary Wirtzenburg (sp?) book called "Fiero" It has the entire history of the Fiero program from it's original concept started in 1978.<P>Some big libraries carry the book too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||03-16-2001||06:34 PM||||I remember seeing something real detailed out there somewhere.  Meanwhile there's a little information on Lisa's site...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/info.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/info.html</A> <P>Found a little more at <A HREF="http://www.fieros.homestead.com/history.html" TARGET=_blank>www.fieros.homestead.com/history.html</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 03-16-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000003||TheFiero64||03-16-2001||06:42 PM||||The Fiero is believed to be the first production car to employ a space-frame chassis. It was also the first Indy Pace Car in exactly 70 years to employ only 4 cylinders. The 2.7 liter power plant could develop 232 HP at 6,500 rpm, & was able to consistently turl laps in excess of 130mph.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierosound||03-25-2001||01:29 PM||||here's a good brief article  <A HREF="http://members.aol.com/topfiero/fiero.txt" TARGET=_blank>http://members.aol.com/topfiero/fiero.txt</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000005||batboy||03-25-2001||02:09 PM||||Look up old car magazine articles on microfilm in the library. I think about fall of 83 there were several in (I'm thinking) Motor Trend or Car and Driver or something like that. They explained the development and how they were made. I have photocopies of those articles, but can't find them right now.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||rogergarrison||03-25-2001||04:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TheFiero64:<BR><B>The Fiero is believed to be the first production car to employ a space-frame chassis. It was also the first Indy Pace Car in exactly 70 years to employ only 4 cylinders. The 2.7 liter power plant could develop 232 HP at 6,500 rpm, & was able to consistently turl laps in excess of 130mph.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>technicaly, first 'US' production car with spaceframe construction. Mercedes and Maserati did it in early 50's (Gullwing, Birdcage)||||reg||1
Z||000007||Standard||03-26-2001||12:14 AM||||It was the first mid-engine car to ever pace the indy 500, and If I remember right it could turn laps at 140 mph with no problem.||||reg||1
Z||000008||WKDFIRO||03-26-2001||04:23 PM||||Check out this address and explore the rest of the website its really chocked full of information.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fierodrivers.com/magazines/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierodrivers.com/magazines/index.html</A> <P>Fiero by Witzenburg is the bible of Fiero information so far out there!||||reg||1
